// DAP (step 6.1): bytecode listings. A NewtonScript function on the stack
// without a source file gets a virtual source (sourceReference) with its
// disassembly, one instruction per line; stack frames point at a line: the
// newest at the instruction that runs next, the callers at their call.
// Breakpoints set in a listing (setBreakpoints with the sourceReference)
// are breakpoints at those instructions; a new set replaces the old one,
// a line past the end is not verified. Functions with a line table (-dap
// compiles with -g) point at their source file instead (step 8.1); Add
// and Work are compiled from strings (Compile), which have no file, so
// they keep their listings.
DefGlobalFn('Add, call Compile("func(a, b) a + b") with ());
DefGlobalFn('Work, call Compile("func(x) begin local y := Add(x, 1); y * 2; end") with ());

InstallBreakPoint(functions.Work, 0);
Print(Work(10));
Print(Work(20));
Print(Work(30));
